@@name
config
@@description
Make the configuration, dependency, build or CI change described in the user request, keeping every environment working.
@@requirements
    - Identify every place the setting or dependency is declared or pinned (lockfiles, CI, containers, docs)
    - Regenerate lockfiles with the project's package manager, never by hand
    - Note any breaking changes from upstream release notes for version bumps
@@approach
    Before editing, reason through:
    - Which environments consume this configuration (local, CI, production)
    - How to roll the change back if it breaks one of them
    Commit to the change set and apply it in one pass.
@@verification
    - Run the project's install and build steps from a fresh checkout (no cached dependencies) and confirm they succeed
@@constraints
    - No secrets or credentials committed to the repository
    - Keep unrelated dependency versions unchanged
@@out-of-scope
    - Upgrading other dependencies that are not named in the request
